## 5. Termination

### 5.1.
The rights granted under this License will terminate automatically if You fail to comply with any of its terms. However, if You become compliant, then the rights granted by this License from a particular Contributor are reinstated: **(a)** provisionally, unless and until such Contributor explicitly or implicitly terminates Your grants, or **(b)** on an ongoing basis, if such Contributor fails to notify You of the non-compliance by some reasonable means prior to 60 days after You have come back into compliance.

### 5.2.
Notwithstanding the above, if You become compliant, then the rights granted by this License from a particular Contributor are reinstated on an ongoing basis if such Contributor notifies You of the non-compliance by some reasonable means, this is the first time You have received notice of non-compliance for this Covered Software from such Contributor, and You become compliant prior to 30 days after Your receipt of the notice.

### 5.3.
If You initiate litigation against any entity by claiming that the Contributor Version or Covered Software infringes a patent (excluding declaratory judgment actions, counter-claims, and cross-claims) alleging that a Contributor Version directly or indirectly infringes any patent, then the rights granted to You by any and all Contributors for the Covered Software under Section 2.1 of this License shall terminate.

### 5.4.
In the event of termination under Sections 5.1, 5.2, or 5.3 above, all end user license agreements (excluding distributors and resellers) which have been validly granted by You or Your distributors under this License prior to termination shall survive termination.

